Subject: [PATCH 3/9] fix(acceptance): what the catalogue already checks is not
 a table column
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Red at 917c70e (culprit 76f66a5d, PR #90):
  nothing-is-done-until-it-is-proven › the rejected English branch also discloses the judge boundary
  Expected "0 of 3 requested criteria were proven", received "0 of 6 …":
    ❌ a column «counter» / «title» / «production build» exists in the table

Root cause: 76f66a5d let a natural-language field list survive the generic
suppression (`!hasExplicitRecordSchema(t)`), so it could feed filter criteria
for «Build a maintenance register with …». hasExplicitRecordSchema is true for
any build request listing two or more things, including «Create a page with a
counter, title, and production build.». The only guard left was uiOnlyLabel,
a closed list of UI words of its own (counter, button, title, heading, status
message) that did not know `production build` — which the acceptance
CATALOGUE checks as a verification — nor the Arabic article («العداد»). Two
readers of one question, and they disagreed: three criteria no page can meet.

Decision: R. The count is derived from the request (law 4), so the count was a
behaviour change. The widget guard now asks the catalogue itself: a derived
label that, read alone, raises a catalogue criterion THIS request already
carries is that criterion and not a column. No second vocabulary. The
culprit's own cases stay green (reading log / maintenance register keep their
columns and filters; widget lists stay suppressed). New cases: NEGATIVE (the
page request; the Arabic-article widgets, which the old list also missed) and
POSITIVE (title, author, rating keeps all three columns).

Measured over the 29 suites that call acceptanceFor/judgeAcceptance/
acceptanceBlock: 26 pass; the 7 failures (a-page-he-named-is-a-criterion…,
a-page-he-never-chose…, media-review-contract) are failing identically at
917c70e and belong to other groups.

Mutations (acceptance.ts, CRLF-mixed; byte-exact tool; sha256 identical):
  acc1 old widget list restored  -> 3 ✕: + "column:text1","column:title","column:text3" (both
       NEGATIVEs) and Expected "0 of 3 …" Received "⚠️ Delivery blocked: 0 of 6 …"
  acc2 every -> some             -> POSITIVE ✕: - "title","author","rating"

Not fixed here (routing, reported): the same hasExplicitRecordSchema makes
deterministicPhasesFor route «Create a page with a counter, title, and
production build.» to react_project (Application) although
classifyBuildScope says page.

